From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Seo <alexandre-seo@example.net>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 17:35:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Fix VLA size in setreg_store for DX010

Increase size of clone array to accommodate null terminator.

Signed-off-by: Alexandre Seo <alexandre-seo@example.net>

Cherry-picked unchanged from sonic-net/sonic-buildimage#26983 (open, base
master), head 894c85517024a8807adc6fe76621b95bbf139563, onto 202511: the
upstream fix for sonic-net/sonic-buildimage#26885 (a 202511 DX010 panics in
dx010_cpld's setreg_store under the 6.12 kernel's FORTIFY_SOURCE when
watchdogutil writes setreg, and boot-loops), taken as submitted so this
image tests what upstream is reviewing.
---
 .../sonic-platform-modules-cel/dx010/modules/dx010_cpld.c       | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-cel/dx010/modules/dx010_cpld.c b/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-cel/dx010/modules/dx010_cpld.c
index d4c15eca9..b0d17c3b9 100644
--- a/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-cel/dx010/modules/dx010_cpld.c
+++ b/platform/broadcom/sonic-platform-modules-cel/dx010/modules/dx010_cpld.c
@@ -190,7 +190,7 @@ static ssize_t setreg_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *devattr
     uint16_t addr;
     uint8_t value;
     char *tok;
-    char clone[count];
+    char clone[count + 1];
     char *pclone = clone;
     char *last;
 
-- 
2.39.5

